<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A post's plane, once the card stopped being a card.

  The feed used to be a stack of MaterialCardViews: a 16dp radius, a fill, and 8dp of margin above
  and below every row, so the content the reader came for sat inside a box and the page read as a
  column of tiles. REDESIGN.md rules that out twice over - "no stock Material demo look", and
  "tonal surfaces instead of hard borders for cards" - and asks for content that owns the frame.

  So this is a plain rectangle: one fill, no radius, no stroke, no elevation. The rows are separated
  by the hairline the layout draws at the foot of each one instead of by a gap between boxes, which
  is what lets two posts share an edge without reading as two panels.

  The fill is unread's tonal step and is deliberately kept as a drawable rather than left to the
  theme's card attributes, because the adapter repaints it on every bind to signal read state: a read
  post is pointed one step down the ramp to colorSurfaceContainerLow, which in this theme is very
  nearly the page background. That is what makes "what you have not read" the lifted plane and
  everything else recede into the page. The tint call works on any view that has a background, which
  is why dropping MaterialCardView does not cost the read state.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="?attr/colorSurfaceContainerHigh" />
</shape>
